#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-log.md:6
msgid "Name"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-log.md:8
msgid ""
"`nix log` - show the build log of the specified packages or paths, if "
"available"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-log.md:10
msgid "Synopsis"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-log.md:12
msgid "`nix log` \\[_option_...\\] _installable_"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-log.md:14
msgid "Examples"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-log.md:16
msgid "Get the build log of GNU Hello:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-log.md:22
msgid "Get the build log of a specific store path:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-log.md:28
msgid "Get a build log from a specific binary cache:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-log.md:30
msgid ""
"```console\n"
"# nix log --store https://cache.nixos.org nixpkgs#hello\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-log.md:34
msgid "Description"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-log.md:36
msgid ""
"This command prints the log of a previous build of the [_installable_](./nix."
"md#installables) on standard output."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-log.md:38
msgid "Nix looks for build logs in two places:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-log.md:40
msgid ""
"In the directory `/nix/var/log/nix/drvs`, which contains logs for locally "
"built derivations."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-log.md:42
msgid ""
"In the binary caches listed in the `substituters` setting. Logs should be "
"named `<cache>/log/<store-path-base-name>`, where `<store-path-base-name>` "
"is the [store path base name](../../store/store-path.md#base-name) of a "
"derivation, e.g. `https://cache.nixos.org/log/"
"dvmig8jgrdapvbyxb1rprckdmdqx08kv-hello-2.10.drv`. For non-derivation store "
"paths, Nix will first try to determine the deriver from the [store object "
"metadata](../../store/store-object.md#metadata)."
msgstr ""

